notes: >
  Gitignored paths are the gate's legal workspace (D-STACK-017): gates run in the real tree, so a
  build cache is readable AND writable with no declarations — the reason repeat runs stay warm on
  path-keyed toolchains (Xcode, Gradle). The gate here both reads the ignored cache and writes
  into it; the write is a cache write, not a VIOLATION, and the guard never resets ignored paths.
  Ignored-only dirt also does not trip the clean-tree precondition.
dirty:
  cache/data.txt: "warm\n"
argv: ['--all']
exitCode: 0
ok: true
gates:
  anystack:needs-cache: { status: pass }
